        "title": "Orbital Mechanics and the Rocket Equation",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Orbital mechanics is the application of Newtonian gravity and classical mechanics to spacecraft trajectories. The Tsiolkovsky rocket equation is the fundamental constraint; Kepler's laws govern orbits; the Hohmann transfer is the minimum-energy path between orbits."
